# Docker build context.
#
# The `server` arm of both bench harnesses builds with the REPO ROOT as its
# context (`bench/parity/Dockerfile.ocserve` does `COPY . /src`). That sent
# 3.57 GB per build, and on 2026-10-27 it failed outright:
#
#   #38 ERROR: error from sender: open .../bench/snapshot-it/data:
#       permission denied
#
# because a scratch directory left behind by an earlier containerised run is
# root-owned (the containers run as root and write into bind mounts). A
# root-owned scratch dir inside a build context is not a harness bug to work
# around with sudo: it is state that must never be in the context at all.
#
# Everything below is either not needed to compile the workspace (benchmarks,
# recorded corpora, fuzz corpus, safety backups, local runs) or is
# machine-local state that would make the image non-reproducible.

target/
.git/

# Benchmarks and their scratch state. Nothing under bench/ or testdata/ is
# compiled into the binary: the only include_str!/include_bytes! assets live
# under crates/*/assets or crates/*/testdata (guard rule 30 enforces crate
# containment), so excluding them cannot break the build.
bench/
mutants.out*/
fuzz/

# Local safety backups (pre-migration VACUUM INTO snapshots). Large, private,
# and unrelated to any build.
.safety/

# Harness outputs and local runs that can be enormous and are not sources.
**/.runs/
**/.runs-archive-*/
**/work/
**/freeze-work/
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm

# Editor/OS noise.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
